{"name":"Punga","hex":"#534931","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"punga","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Alternative form of ponga."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/punga"}],"entries":[{"title":"Punga (mythology)","blocks":[{"text":"In Māori mythology, Punga is a supernatural being, the ancestor of sharks, lizards, rays, and all deformed, ugly things. All ugly and strange animals are Punga's children. Hence the saying Te aitanga a Punga used to describe an ugly person."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Manta_birostris-Thailand3.jpg/330px-Manta_birostris-Thailand3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Punga_(mythology)","wikidata":"Q4383732"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Manta_birostris-Thailand3.jpg/500px-Manta_birostris-Thailand3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4b/Manta_birostris-Thailand3.jpg/500px-Manta_birostris-Thailand3.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Strange animals, such as this manta ray, are Punga's children.","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AManta_birostris-Thailand3.jpg"}],"sounds":{}}}